      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T08:30:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note this means the QueryTask should be run immediately immediately after being created (not be scheduled in advance). Because the result of \"makeResponsesForResolveIfUnknown\" depends on answers that were received before it is called, so to take into account all answers before sending the query, it needs to be called just before sending it.\n\nOtherwise, you\u0027d end up with:\n - First QueryTask is created, mDNS query sent\n - Next QueryTask is scheduled for 1s later. There\u0027s still no known response for the service, so an incomplete resolve response is created.\n - Service replies after 100ms\n - 900ms later, second QueryTask is run, but it doesn\u0027t take into the account the earlier reply.\n \nWhat should happen is:\n - First QueryTask is created, mDNS query sent\n - Message is scheduled to create the next QueryTask in 1s\n - Service replies after 100ms\n - 900ms later, second QueryTask is created, and uses the last reply data. Then it\u0027s executed immediately on the Executor.",
      "revId": "7f6b73198b9654c6389b12ad796c197131edccff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
