      "writtenOn": "2023-05-10T08:30:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is racy because now stopSendAndReceive could cancel the requestTaskFuture after handler.post was called, but before the handler executed this block. Then requestTaskFuture gets re-scheduled when the handler executes this block, so the \"cancel\" didn\u0027t work and discovery keeps running.\n\nI think you could:\n\n - Take a looper as argument instead of Handler for in the MdnsServiceTypeClient constructor\n - Use a subclass of Handler that overrides handleMessage. It would call executor.submit with a new QueryTask every time a new message (MSG_START_QUERYTASK ?) is processed; and probably do the \"remove service after TTL expires\" thing too.\n - Instead of handler.post here, use handler.sendMessageDelayed with MSG_START_QUERYTASK\n - Delete requestTaskFuture. Use handler.removeMessages to cancel pending tasks instead, making sure that it is called from the handler thread.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 574,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 574,
        "endChar": 37
      },
